Use importlib.metadata to read openstacksdk version.

openstacksdk has dropped its internal import of the deprecated
openstack.version submodule (commit 3ae89d61 "drop deprecated
openstack.version", 2026-06-02). That import was the side effect
that made openstack.version reachable as an attribute on the
openstack package; with it gone, any consumer that reads
openstack.version.__version__ now fails with:

    AttributeError: module 'openstack' has no attribute 'version'

This collection hit that failure in three places:

* plugins/module_utils/openstack.py (legacy
    openstack_cloud_from_module function)
* plugins/module_utils/openstack.py (OpenStackModule class)
* plugins/inventory/openstack.py

Switch all three call sites to conditionally import
importlib.metadata.version and packaging, as these are not in the
Lint sanity requirements file. Then call to get base_version,
which is the canonical Python way of reading an installed
distribution's version and will omit pbr generated versioning like
"1.1.1.dev11".

